8.jpg 500w, https://64.media.tumblr.com/0556f40afbddc65d96ebed6d036fb350/47be743c66431029-1e/s540x810/35376b725073447f5a9dd7f52f2a9dba0af9b28d.jpg 540w, https://64.media.tumblr.com/0556f40afbddc65d96ebed6d036fb350/47be743c66431029-1e/s640x960/1264f5454baad6756ad4f33ce454398d0cce0d72.jpg 640w, https://64.media.tumblr.com/0556f40afbddc65d96ebed6d036fb350/47be743c66431029-1e/s1280x1920/8daf8d49426add489be3b9336d30150fcb513998.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px\"/></figure></div><p>The other day, one of our network switches broken, and just wouldn&rsquo;t turn on. We had a replacement in storage, but couldn&rsquo;t get us to throw the old one out. Turns out it was just a broken capacitor, which is a 5 minutes, 20cents fix. After replacing the broken one, the whole thing works again. So now we have a new replacement switch when the next one breaks 😁</p>",
